1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
The most used word on Earth
was invented as a joke.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:08,500
In the 1830s, Boston newspaper writers
had a trend of abbreviating misspelled phrases.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:13,500
OK stood for "oll korrect" —
a playful misspelling of "all correct."

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:19,000
It started as slang, spread through
telegraph operators who loved its brevity,

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
and now it's understood
in virtually every language.

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,000
Follow for more language secrets
hiding in plain sight.
